From: mjb-is <mjb-is@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:57:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 096/123] Read unencrypted snapshots with an encryption key
 loaded

With a key configured for a server, every chunk the readers fetched was
checked against the keyed digest (sha256 of the plaintext and id_key), so
the server's older unencrypted snapshots, whose index holds plain sha256
digests, failed with "content hash mismatch": Restore, Undelete and Roll
back could not read anything taken before the key was set up. Found live on
winclient: an Undelete scan of a machine set over encrypted and unencrypted
snapshots.

DIDXReaderAt (which also reads fixed indexes) uses ChunkMatchesDigest, and
DecodeBlob's unencrypted cases verifyUnencryptedDigest: with a key loaded a
plain sha256 match is accepted as well as the keyed one. A chunk matching
the other kind of digest would need a sha256 preimage, so nothing is
weakened; encrypted blobs keep the strict keyed check.

Fork adaptation: ChunkMatchesDigest replaces the fork's narrower
legacyEncryptedDigest (bd164c1): the same plain-sha256 acceptance with a
key loaded, which also covers the encrypted snapshots the 0.4.1/0.4.2 GUI
indexed under the plain digest (issue #13). The fork's reader has no
hash timing, and its CHANGELOG is kept.

